# package-lock.json is committed: this app is vendored, installs must be reproducible

.idea

# The Sketchfab source model (135 MB) IS committed, despite this rule.
#
# The rule was added after those files were already tracked, and .gitignore
# has no effect on tracked files — so the intent recorded here ("only the
# compressed output ships") never actually took hold. That was checked, not
# assumed: `git ls-files assets/madring-sketchfab/` lists scene.bin, scene.gltf
# and 60 textures.
#
# It is left committed deliberately. Untracking them now would NOT make clones
# any smaller — the blobs stay in history, so `git clone` still transfers them
# — it would only remove the benefit of a clone being self-sufficient. Anyone
# can clone this repo and re-run the whole asset pipeline without a Sketchfab
# account. Redistribution is fine under CC-BY-4.0 as long as attribution is
# given, which it is (see NOTICE, and the on-screen credit in the intro).
#
# HAZARD if you ever re-export the model: scene.bin is 97.7 MiB and GitHub's
# hard per-file limit is 100 MiB. There is 2.3 MiB of headroom. A re-export
# that grows it past that will make the push fail outright, and the fix at
# that point is Git LFS or a history rewrite, not a bigger commit.
#
# What the games actually load at runtime is far smaller, and both derivatives
# are committed too: public/models/circuit-draco.glb (8.9 MB) for the 3D mode
# and ../images/madring-overhead.jpg (1.1 MB) for the 2D one. See
# `npm run build:assets` for how the source turns into those.
/assets/madring-sketchfab
